Disabling the debug function on ttyTCU0 on a Jetson Orin device primarily involves preventing the console output from being directed to this serial port. This can be achieved by modifying the boot arguments.
Steps to disable debug console on ttyTCU0:
Edit extlinux.conf: Access the extlinux.conf file, typically located at /boot/extlinux/extlinux.conf on your Jetson Orin device. This file contains the kernel command-line arguments used during boot.
Remove console=ttyTCU0,115200: Within the APPEND line of your chosen boot entry in extlinux.conf, locate and remove the string console=ttyTCU0,115200. This argument directs the kernel's console output to the ttyTCU0 serial port at a baud rate of 115200. Removing it will prevent the kernel from sending its messages to this port.
Code

    # Example extlinux.conf snippet
    LABEL primary
        MENU LABEL primary kernel
        LINUX /boot/Image
        INITRD /boot/initrd
        APPEND ${cbootargs} quiet root=/dev/mmcblk0p1 rw rootwait console=ttyTCU0,115200n8
Modify the APPEND line to remove console=ttyTCU0,115200n8 (or similar).
Reboot the device: After saving the changes to extlinux.conf, reboot your Jetson Orin device for the modifications to take effect.

